				\begin{document}$$\begin{aligned} x_{i,d} = lb_{d} + (ub_{d}-lb_{d}) \times r, i=1,2,3..N, d =1,2,3..D \end{aligned}$$\end{document}xi,d=lbd+(ubd-lbd)×r,i=1,2,3..N,d=1,2,3..D Where N is the population size, D is the number of variables that are designed, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
