Figure 4 displays particle trajectories and convergence curves for some CEC 2017 benchmark functions, demonstrating the effectiveness of hybrid algorithms. The convergence curves demonstrate efficient exploration and exploitation by showing an initial fitness improvement followed by fine-tuning. The trajectory of the particles shows a starting motion convergent to center areas, demonstrating the algorithm’s capacity to balance exploration and exploitation across several functions. In general, the method performs well when optimizing these benchmark functions.Table 3
